From fea5e7d5425c36df1c9bbb81800a9caaffe64bb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lonewolf0622 <hoseinxmusic@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:25:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] radv/bc250: DirectMesh v1.3 mesh and task shaders for GFX1013

VK_EXT_mesh_shader (Mesh + Task) and VK_KHR_fragment_shader_barycentric on
the BC-250, plus (v1.2) VK_EXT_device_generated_commands for Mesh/Task draws,
multiview with Mesh shaders, and indirect Task draws whose rarely used extra
chunks are recorded once per call, and (v1.3) indexed Mesh draws, where
eligible Mesh-only triangle pipelines run their index work as compute and
draw with ordinary indexed draws, all drawn on a safe direct path: one launch per Mesh workgroup, no
split/replay, and an export chosen per workgroup that rules out the index
patterns that hang this chip. An automatic converter rewrites application
Mesh/Task shaders into a form that path accepts; anything nothing can prove
safe takes the older split/expansion path or is refused at pipeline
creation, never the raw route. Enabled per game with RADV_DIRECTMESH=1,
and it only ever affects GFX1013.

Author's validation (real hardware, RADV_DIRECTMESH=1), v1.1:
dEQP-VK.mesh_shader.ext.* plus the fragment-barycentric Mesh cases that run
on this device, 3,558/3,558 pass with 0 hangs; 10,036 more Mesh/Task-stage
cases in other groups pass. Games: Final Fantasy VII Rebirth, Control,
Hellblade 2 and Alan Wake 2 run with Mesh direct. v1.2 adds byte-identical
image checks against the proven route for device-generated Mesh and Task draws,
descriptor buffers with device-generated commands, graphics pipeline libraries
and shader objects with Mesh, and indirect Task draws large enough to need the
extra chunks; Crimson Desert runs with Mesh shaders on. v1.3:
dEQP-VK.mesh_shader.* 1,902/1,902 including all multiview cases, image
checks against vertex-shader references, indirect-pool overflow, storage
exhaustion and command-buffer reuse with no GPU faults; meshlets of 96+
vertices draw about 1.5-1.9x faster than v1.2 through the indexed route.

Source: https://github.com/lonewolf0622/bc250meshtaskwork, release
directmesh-v1.3 (commit a2428cb), patches/bc250-directmesh-mesa-26.2.1.patch
sha256 b5b4a49035df5542d20f239320b1caed30dd8cd911925bf38aecb83848cdd779.

Changes on top of upstream (this repository): RADV_DIRECTMESH=1 is made the one
opt-in for everything the series changes by default. Upstream also
exposes mesh/task shaders, fragment shader barycentrics and a no-op
VK_KHR_fragment_shading_rate on every GFX1013 device, and changed the
winsys IB reuse there, whether or not the switch was set - and without the
switch the fail-closed direct-path checks are not filled in. Here
bc250_native_mesh, bc250_barycentrics, bc250_vrs_noop and the IB retention
all require radv_bc250_directmesh_requested() (RADV_DIRECTMESH exactly
"1", the same test radv_bc250_directmesh_env uses), so without the switch a
GFX1013 device exposes what the base driver exposes. The comment claiming
mesh is exposed through RADV_PERFTEST=mesh is corrected: there is no such
perftest flag (unknown names are ignored); the switch's only RADV_PERFTEST
effect is turning on nircache when RADV_PERFTEST is unset.

The two v1.2 fixes this repository carried are upstream as of v1.3: the
DXVK carve-out (DXVK keeps graphics pipeline libraries while the preset turns
hybrid Task on) is decided on the first vkCreateInstance only, and
BC250_CAPTURE_POINTERS is read once instead of with getenv on every state
flush on every GPU.

v1.3 calls radv_bc250_idx_restore() at the top of radv_before_draw and
radv_before_taskmesh_draw. It lives in another file, so every draw on every
GPU paid a call to find the index route inactive; here the two hot paths
test cmd_buffer->bc250_idx_restore inline first. Behaviour is unchanged.

Replaces this repository's earlier 0002-0004 (the RADV_GFX103 experimental
mesh/task path, which in practice only worked for Final Fantasy VII
Rebirth).

The two src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c hunks that expose the GFX1013 compute
queue and route it through the async-compute threadgroup workaround are
dropped: they are identical in code to 0001, which carries them.

Rebased from Mesa 26.2.1 onto 26.2.4 (via 26.2.3). Three real conflicts.

In 26.2.3:
src/amd/vulkan/radv_pipeline_cache.c, where 26.2.3 backported upstream's
fix for the same bug DirectMesh fixed independently (9679ac6cf19, hash
descriptor set layouts in radv_hash_graphics_spirv_to_nir). DirectMesh's
version is kept: it also hashes which set slots are empty, so {L, NULL}
and {NULL, L} no longer share a key, and it is the version that was
validated on hardware.

In 26.2.4, two backports land on code v1.2 changes, resolved as on Mesa main
(v1.3's radv_bc250_idx_restore() call goes in front of 26.2.4's version of
CmdBindShadersEXT):
- 4574e63f1dd ("fix dirtying graphics shaders when shader objects are
  bound") already marks graphics shaders dirty only when graphics stages
  are bound, which is what v1.2's bound_stages logic in CmdBindShadersEXT
  does; upstream's version is kept, so the function is identical to 26.2.4.
- 0209c5a8b13 ("fix checking whether a FS is present") makes the
  fragment-shading-rate strip require fs_stage->nir; the bc250_vrs_noop
  backstop stays outside that check, so it still covers pipelines without
  a fragment shader.

